{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And for the tribe of Dan, a prince.</b> The reason he did not write 'prince' for the tribe of Judah, Simeon, and Benjamin is that Caleb was already called the servant of HaShem in the matter of the spies, and stood in his righteousness all the days of his life, and therefore he did not need to call him prince. For Benjamin too it is written 'Eldad' — he is Eldad, the companion of Medad, who was a prophet and as distinguished as a prince. Another interpretation: because he is destined to do the deed of the concubine at Gibeah, he is not called prince. And for Simeon, because they gathered together in the matter of Zimri, as Rashi explained in the portion of Balak, and caused a stumbling for Israel. For the tribe of Reuben and the tribe of Gad he did not need to, for they had already taken their portion in the land of Sihon and Og. He arranged them in this order, for it is neither according to birth order nor according to the standards nor according to seniority."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:42.375629155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}